\pard\li1800\b API \b0\par
\pard\fi-720\li3240\b jsonpickle.encode \b0 (value, unpicklable=True, make_refs=True, keys=False, max_depth=None, reset=True, backend=None, warn=False, context=None, max_iter=None, numeric_keys=False)\par
\pard\li3240 Return a JSON formatted representation of value, a Python object.\par
Parameters:\tab\par
\pard\fi-1170\li4410\cf8 unpicklable\tab If set to False then the output will not contain the information necessary to turn the JSON data back into Python objects, but a simpler JSON stream is produced.\par
max_depth\tab If set to a non-negative integer then jsonpickle will not recurse deeper than \lquote max_depth\rquote  steps into the object. Anything deeper than \lquote max_depth\rquote  is represented using a Python repr() of the object.\par
make_refs\tab If set to False jsonpickle\rquote s referencing support is disabled. Objects that are id()-identical won\rquote t be preserved across encode()/decode(), but the resulting JSON stream will be conceptually simpler. jsonpickle detects cyclical objects and will break the cycle by calling repr() instead of recursing when make_refs is set False.\par
\cf2 keys\tab If set to True then jsonpickle will encode non-string dictionary keys instead of coercing them into strings via repr().\par
\cf8 warn\tab If set to True then jsonpickle will warn when it returns None for an object which it cannot pickle (e.g. file descriptors).\par
max_iter\tab If set to a non-negative integer then jsonpickle will consume at most max_iter items when pickling iterators.\cf2\par
\pard\li3240\par
\pard\fi-720\li3240\b jsonpickle.decode\b0 (string, backend=None, context=None, keys=False, reset=True, safe=False, classes=None)\par
\pard\li3240 Convert a JSON string into a Python object.\par
\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li3600 The keyword argument \lquote keys\rquote  defaults to False. If set to True then jsonpickle will decode non-string dictionary keys into python objects via the jsonpickle protocol.\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}The keyword argument \lquote classes\rquote  defaults to None. If set to a single class, or a sequence (list, set, tuple) of classes, then the classes will be made available when constructing objects. This can be used to give jsonpickle access to local classes that are not available through the global module import scope.\par
