\pard\li720 Python Objects and QVariant\par
\b0\par
\pard\li1440 Qt uses the QVariant class as a wrapper for any C++ data type. PyQt allows any Python object to be wrapped as a QVariant and passed around Qt's meta-object system like any other type.\par
PyQt will try to convert the Python object to a C++ equivalent if it can so that the QVariant can be passed to other C++ code that doesn't know what a Python object is.\par
Version 2 of PyQt's QVariant API will automatically convert a QVariant back to a Python object of the correct type.\par
Version 1 of the QVariant API provides the QVariant.toPyObject() method to convert the QVariant back to a Python object of the correct type.\par
Both versions will raise a Python exception if the conversion cannot be done.\par
